$$SYNTAX-LEVEL 2
*(mgdb-blast
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary">
<meta name="twitter:site" content="@MaizeGDB">
<meta property="og:url" content="https://maizegdb.org/BLAST">
<meta property="og:title" content="MaizeGDB BLAST | Search maize sequence">
<meta property="og:description" content="BLAST a nucleotide or protein sequence against maize and Zea genome assemblies, gene models, transcripts and proteins at MaizeGDB.">

<main class="mgdb-page mgdb-hub-page mgdb-blast-page" id="blast-main">
  <nav class="mgdb-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span><a href="/sitemap">Tools</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span><span aria-current="page">BLAST</span>
  </nav>

  <section class="mgdb-hero" aria-labelledby="blast-title">
    <div class="mgdb-hero-emblem">
      <svg class="blast-hero-mark" viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="A query sequence aligned against a target">
        <g fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="9">
          <path d="M14 30h92" stroke="#501719" />
          <path d="M14 60h34" stroke="#2f5e2a" /><path d="M58 60h48" stroke="#2f5e2a" />
          <path d="M14 90h92" stroke="#a96919" />
        </g>
        <g fill="#f4edd0"><circle cx="53" cy="60" r="6" /></g>
        <g fill="none" stroke="#8a5a0f" stroke-width="4" stroke-dasharray="5 6">
          <path d="M30 34v22M74 34v22M40 64v22M88 64v22" />
        </g>
      </svg>
      <strong>MaizeGDB<br />BLAST</strong>
    </div>
    <div class="mgdb-hero-body">
      <h1 id="blast-title">Search maize sequence.</h1>
      <p class="mgdb-hero-description">Search sequence from all genome datasets hosted by MaizeGDB.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="mgdb-section-tabs" aria-label="Sections on this page">
    <a href="#blast-search" class="is-current" aria-current="true">Search</a>
    <a href="#blast-about">About</a>
    <a href="#blast-references">References</a>
    <a href="#blast-related">Related resources</a>
  </nav>

  <section id="blast-search" aria-labelledby="blast-search-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="blast-search-title">Search</h2></div>
    </div>

    <p class="blast-search-lead">Three steps. The current B73 assembly is already selected, so a sequence and a press of Run BLAST is a complete search.</p>

    ;; The form is three numbered steps built from the site's own controls. Every
    ;; control id, name and class in it is what controllers/BLAST/BLAST.js
    ;; already drives -- that script and the job submission path behind it are
    ;; untouched. The wrapper carries no styling of its own now that the form is
    ;; not a nested page.
    *(blast-form)
  </section>

  <section id="blast-about" class="mgdb-prose-layout" aria-labelledby="blast-about-title">
    <div class="mgdb-prose">
      <h2 id="blast-about-title" class="mgdb-leaf-heading">About</h2>
      <p>BLAST finds regions of local similarity between your query and a target dataset, and reports each one with an alignment, a bit score and an E&#8209;value. A low E&#8209;value means a match that is unlikely to have arisen by chance in a database of that size &#8212; it is not a measure of biological relevance, which is yours to judge.</p>
      <p>You do not choose a program. The query sequence type and the target you pick decide it: a nucleotide query against a nucleotide target runs <code>blastn</code>, a protein query against a protein target <code>blastp</code>, and the mixed cases run <code>blastx</code> or <code>tblastn</code>. The parameter set defaults to values suited to that pairing, and every one of them can be overridden.</p>
      <p>Searches run as jobs. A job keeps its results under a job identifier, so a long search can be left and returned to, and a finished search can be reopened later from the same address.</p>
    </div>
    <!-- The "Search by identifier" button went when this copy arrived: the Gene
         Data Hub is a link in the second line now, and a button repeating it
         under three sentences that each carry their own destination read as a
         fourth option rather than a shortcut. -->
    <aside class="mgdb-aside-card">
      <h3>Choose the right tool</h3>
      <p>Use BLAST to find sequences that match your sequence.</p>
      <p>Already have a gene, locus, or marker ID? Use the <a href="/gene_center/gene">Gene Data Hub</a>.</p>
      <p>Want to compare protein structures instead of sequences? Use <a href="/foldseek">Foldseek</a> in the <a href="/data_center/protein_structure">Protein Structure Hub</a>.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section id="blast-references" aria-labelledby="blast-references-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="blast-references-title">References</h2></div>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-ref-list">
      $(reference_cards)
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="blast-related" class="mgdb-hub-related" aria-labelledby="blast-related-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div>
        <h2 id="blast-related-title">Related resources</h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-resource-panel">
      <div class="mgdb-resource-list">
        <a href="/gene_center/gene">
          <strong>Gene Data Hub</strong>
          <span>Resolve a gene model, transcript or translation identifier directly</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/genome">
          <strong>Genome Data Hub</strong>
          <span>The assemblies and annotations these target datasets are built from</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/data_center/protein_structure">
          <strong>Protein structures</strong>
          <span>Foldseek searches structure where BLAST searches sequence</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/genome/genomebrowser">
          <strong>Genome browser</strong>
          <span>Take a hit's coordinates into JBrowse to see what else is there</span>
        </a>
        <a href="https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <strong>NCBI BLAST</strong>
          <span>Search beyond maize, against the whole of GenBank</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
)
